    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d625">

                <pb facs="0916" n="780" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg780"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/3354: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Moore</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-27T12:00:00-05:00">April 27,
                        1929—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>84. My telegram number 83.<anchor n="25" xml:id="d625-f1"/> Saw President Leguia
                    at 11:30 this morning. He said: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Under no circumstances or conditions would I do anything in the
                            slightest way to embarrass President Hoover for whom I have the greatest
                            admiration. I shall ask to have the clause withdrawn immediately.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>He thoroughly agrees with your viewpoint, which he says is most logical. He will
                    see the Chilean Ambassador at 12:30 today. Have you any further instructions or
                    suggestions?</p>
                <p>More to follow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
